From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:18:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 178/182] hjviewer: a Windows clipboard written from the other
 side carries its owner mark first

When text or other content comes in from the other side, HJViewer puts
it on the Windows clipboard together with a mark that says "this came
from HJViewer", so the next clipboard check does not send it back. The
Windows setter empties the clipboard and writes the formats in order,
stopping at the first one that fails; with the mark written last, a
failed format left unmarked content behind. HJViewer then read it as a
new local copy and sent it back, and the other side emptied its own
clipboard for it, which for Excel ends the "copied" state (the moving
border) of a selection the user just copied. The mark now goes first on
Windows, so a partial write is still known as HJViewer's. Other
platforms keep it last; every reader looks for the mark anywhere in the
list.

Backported from rustdesk/rustdesk 8d74ff0e57765f4fab7a4a4ada32f4c38811c5c2 (fix(windows): write the clipboard owner marker first (#16695))
Upstream's diff unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/clipboard.rs | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/clipboard.rs b/src/clipboard.rs
index 9a1bd60..78136a8 100644
--- a/src/clipboard.rs
+++ b/src/clipboard.rs
@@ -281,10 +281,16 @@ fn do_update_clipboard_(mut to_update_data: Vec<ClipboardData>, side: ClipboardS
 
 #[cfg(not(target_os = "android"))]
 fn append_owner_marker(mut data: Vec<ClipboardData>, side: ClipboardSide) -> Vec<ClipboardData> {
-    data.push(ClipboardData::Special((
+    let marker = ClipboardData::Special((
         RUSTDESK_CLIPBOARD_OWNER_FORMAT.to_owned(),
         side.get_owner_data(),
-    )));
+    ));
+    // The Windows setter stops at the first format it fails to write, so a marker placed
+    // last can be skipped, leaving content RustDesk no longer recognizes as its own.
+    #[cfg(target_os = "windows")]
+    data.insert(0, marker);
+    #[cfg(not(target_os = "windows"))]
+    data.push(marker);
     data
 }
 
